<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Reasoning stage: the slow System 2 pass. The cognition
  (abilities/cognition/cognition.scx) invokes it once and holds it for its
  lifetime, as mosfet.py's Cognition holds its Reasoning (decision D269):
  each turn its earlier stages left unhandled is a
  bot.ability.processing.input, answered by one
  bot.ability.processing.output, and a turn the cognition leaves
  (cancelled or timed out) is a bot.ability.processing.cancel, which ends
  the turn in hand unanswered.

  Tiers (one chart that reasoning and intuition share; decision D144): the <param> tier is reasoning, or
  intuition, the chat tier the cognition invokes this chart as when the bot
  composes one. Intuition asks its own model (both tiers ask with
  reasoning_effort none, the generate service's only one with a schema)
  and is offered the
  deliberative handoff,
  bot.ability.reasoning.input, among its choices: selecting it sends the
  stage's other selections, in order, and hands the turn on, its output
  unhandled with what was sent as its acted. The handoff is never sent, and
  a tier not offered it cannot select it (the dispatch tool's schema
  refuses it). Its failures name the tier ("the intuition failed (...)").

    idle -bot.ability.processing.input-> recalling
         -> applying (an invoked generate service) -> done -> idle

  Memory: with a
  memory (the <param> memory, the address of the bot's memory), recalling
  asks the bot's memory (abilities/memory/memory.scx, decision D266) with one
  transaction of two selects, prior cognitive episodes
  (query_tags cognitive_episode) and standing directives (query_tags
  standing_directive), each for the turn's context or none, oldest first,
  at most 50, and sends itself bot.ability.reasoning.recalled with them and
  memory_consulted true. Reasoning writes nothing: the turn's episode is
  stored once, by reflection after the turn's output (decision D97). The
  context is the stimulus's target_device. The recalled rows are read
  with <memory:contents>: a row that is not a JSON object is skipped. A
  memory failure fails the stage ("Reasoning memory recall
  failed: ..."). Without a memory recalling
  logs <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"> and sends its event with
  memory_consulted false and nothing recalled.

  Recall by association (decision D256, mosfet.py's Associative): with a
  memory, recalling first embeds the cue, the words the stimulus
  carries (each message of a text type's content once, at most 2048
  bytes), as a query with the Embedding ability
  (abilities/embedding/embedding.scx), while it selects the candidates, the
  64 newest prior episodes with their vectors (bot_memory_embedding, kind
  text, which reflection stores), and scores each as mosfet.py's
  Associative does: similarity (1) times its cosine with the cue plus
  recency (0.35) times 0.5 to the power of its age before the newest
  candidate over the half-life (2 days); an episode without a vector
  scores by recency alone. The prior episodes recalled are the best,
  ties newer first, that hold at most 24576 characters of content in
  all, read oldest first (logged reasoning.recall: the best three, id and
  cosine). A stimulus without words, or a cue the Embedding ability
  fails (logged reasoning.embedding: the failure's kind), recalls the
  newest episodes as above.

  Prompt (built by <cognition:model_facing_content>): the system message
  is the system channel, its instructions (none: reasoning has no static
  policy, instructions "") then the self block of the
  bot's self (the <param> self, what the cognition was told of itself,
  with the bot's active learned behaviors that recalling read, at most 32
  {name, lifetime, description} by name, so the bot knows what it has
  learned to do and which routines are running, decision D154),
  and is left out when both are empty; the user message is laid out most
  stable first: the recent turns heard and said (the <param> recent, the
  short-term register's, as <memory:turn> lines, uncounted but
  trimmed to the newest that fit the byte budget), the recalled prior_episodes (cognition:cognitive_episode)
  and standing_directives (cognition:directive) after the turn's
  situation (the environment block, decision D106, then what earlier
  stages already did on the turn, the <param> acted, then the <held> block
  of the actions over the tier's effort ceiling, the <param> held, decision
  D206), then the stimulus as
  the root element of its own block, stamped stimulus:event, stimulus:id,
  stimulus:source and stimulus:target. An image the stimulus carries (a
  sight's view, a visual stimulus) renders as its <media:image ref>
  placeholder, and the user message's content is then the text followed by
  each image as an image part, in ref order, so the model sees what the bot
  sees (decision D250). The stimulus's data is JSON here,
  so it renders as plain data: a content field, an object as entry elements, an array as item elements,
  each object or array item filled as one (decision D99), indented by two
  spaces, an empty element written as <name />. The budgets hold: 49152 encoded bytes, 4096
  nodes, 4096 collection items and 65536 characters per scalar for the
  projection; the system channel and the dispatch schema are reserved
  first, and the projection renders into the bytes they leave of the
  prompt's 49152. Recalled context never fails the turn: prior_episodes
  and standing_directives keep their newest items that fit and count the
  rest as omitted="<n>". Over a budget otherwise (the stimulus alone
  overflows), the element writes the budget's message to prompt_failure and the stage fails without a model call with
  it (for example "prompt projection encoded byte budget exceeded").
  applying ends on the generate service's done.invoke. The call streams its reply (its stream <data>, true by
  default, decision D262; with it false, when the run's FLOPPY_STREAM
  says the backend does, env:stream), and each generate.progress the
  service returns while the reply arrives is sent on to the parent
  cognition, whose stage bound is then one of inactivity (decision D101).
  Drafts (decision D262): the call also carries the draft markers of the
  choices that declare one (generate's drafts, {} for none), so a streamed
  call returns, before its result, an event per marked field's new words,
  named by its marker; each goes on, as it arrives, to the one target that
  offers the drafted event (_event.data.event), so a reply can be said
  while it is written. A draft whose event more than one target offers is
  dropped; the result is the selection of record.

  Choices: the body's collected choices for the turn (the <param>
  choices: the body's own and each ability's offers, each tagged with the
  session id of its offerer as target). The dispatch tool is
  built from the choices by <processing:send> and offered as generate's
  one tool, named dispatch: {events: [anyOf one branch per offered
  event]}, each branch {event (a one-value enum), data (the event's
  schema), reason (optional), and target (an enum of the sessions offering
  it)}. The generate service returns the reply's tool calls only once every
  one is a dispatch call whose arguments the tool's schema admits, so a
  selection outside the choices (event, target or data) or a call of
  another tool fails the stage as schema-mismatch before anything is sent.
  With no choices the stage fails
  without a model call.

  Dispatch (decision D113): generate.result's events, of
  every dispatch call in order, are each sent to the session their target
  names (#_scxml_ + target, decision D104) and kept, in order, as the
  stage's selected. A send that fails (error.*) fails the stage. A
  selected bot.ability.cognition.ignore goes to the cognition, which only
  logs it.

  Repair (decision D142): a
  reply the dispatch tool's schema refuses (generate.failed not-json or
  schema-mismatch, its rejection {key, message}, or its code as both
  without one) is not yet a failure: applying is entered again, so the
  call is made again with repair feedback (the rejection
  message, marked as untrusted validator diagnostic data) rendered last
  in the prompt, at most max_selection_repairs (2) times. The same
  rejection key twice running, or a rejection once the repairs are
  spent, fails the stage with "Selection rejected:
  <message>".

  Context fit (decision D143): with a max_context_tokens, each call's prompt is fitted
  to floor((max_context_tokens - completion_reserve_tokens) *
  bytes_per_token) bytes of request, the system channel and the dispatch
  schema included: the prompt renders whole, or with its recalled memory
  trimmed to fit (logged cognition.fit fit, cut or overflow; the stimulus
  is never cut). Each generate.result whose usage counts the input tokens
  of a request of request_bytes teaches bytes_per_token the fewest bytes
  a token any reply showed, and the output carries it back to the
  cognition, which passes it in the next turn's input.

  Input: bot.ability.processing.input {turn, stimulus, focus,
  focus_candidates, choices, held, environment, self, acted, recent,
  max_context_tokens, completion_reserve_tokens, bytes_per_token}; the
  <param>s are tier, model, memory and embedding. A turn starts with
  nothing of the turn before. Output: bot.ability.processing.output, to
  the cognition:

    {turn, handled: true, selected: [{event, data, reason, target}], bytes_per_token}
    {turn, handled: false, reason: "handoff", acted: [{event, data, reason, target}], bytes_per_token}
    {turn, handled: false, failed: true, reason, bytes_per_token}

  The cognition's hop timeout bounds the stage (its cancel leaves the
  turn, which cancels the model call, SCXML 6.4). The model call takes a
  generated invoke id (idlocation), so a cancelled call's late events are
  not the next turn's.

  Bindings: the generate service package, the processing namespace
  (<processing:send> builds the dispatch tool) and the cognition namespace
  (<cognition:model_facing_content> builds the prompt) and the memory
  namespace (<memory:contents> reads the recalled rows), resolved from their
  repository URIs (the bot's memory, which the body invokes, binds the sql
  service); env scopes FLOPPY_API_KEY and
  FLOPPY_BASE_URL to the service's <invoke> (no default backend: without
  a base URL it answers generate.failed unconfigured, and without a key it
  asks a keyless backend with no key header, decision D127). The generate
  service's events are recorded by one transition each.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:cognition="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/cognition"
       xmlns:env="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:memory="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/memory"
       xmlns:processing="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/processing"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="reasoning" initial="idle">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The turn, from the cognition's <param>s. -->
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="stimulus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus_candidates" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="model" expr="'gemma-4-26b-a4b'"/>
    <!-- Whether the call asks for a streamed reply itself (decision D262:
         on by default, so a reply can be said while it is written); false
         leaves it to the run's FLOPPY_STREAM (decision D101). -->
    <data id="stream" expr="true"/>
    <!-- The tier this chart thinks as (decision D144): reasoning, or
         intuition, the chat tier the cognition invokes it as. -->
    <data id="tier" expr="'reasoning'"/>
    <data id="choices" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The actions held from this tier, over its effort ceiling (decision
         D206): {event, description?} each, rendered as the <held> block
         after the acted fact. Intuition can only hand them on to reasoning;
         reasoning holds nothing (its ceiling is the whole frame). -->
    <data id="held" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The bot's environment (decision D106): its prompt renders it as
         the environment block. -->
    <data id="environment" expr="null"/>
    <!-- What the bot knows of itself (the cognition's self datum) and what
         earlier stages already did on the turn (their dispatched
         selections), from the cognition's <param>s. -->
    <data id="self" expr="null"/>
    <data id="acted" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The recent turns heard and said (the short-term register's, from
         the cognition), rendered first, uncounted, and trimmed to the
         newest that fit. -->
    <data id="recent" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- Reasoning's static policy: none. -->
    <data id="instructions" expr="''"/>
    <!-- The system channel <cognition:model_facing_content> writes, null for
         none. -->
    <data id="system" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The model call: its schema, invocation, and reply. -->
    <data id="schema" expr="null"/>
    <data id="prompt" expr="null"/>
    <data id="prompt_failure" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The references of the images the stimulus carries, sent as image
         parts after the prompt (decision D250). -->
    <data id="images" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="selected" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Whether the selections held the deliberative handoff. -->
    <data id="handed_on" expr="false"/>
    <data id="gen_failure" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Selection repair (decision D142): the rejection of this attempt
         ({key, message}), the attempts repaired so far (at most
         max_selection_repairs), the key of the rejection just before, and
         the feedback the next attempt renders last. -->
    <data id="rejection" expr="null"/>
    <data id="attempt" expr="0"/>
    <data id="max_selection_repairs" expr="2"/>
    <data id="last_rejection_key" expr="null"/>
    <data id="feedback" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Context fit (decision D143): the model's
         context and the tokens reserved for its reply, from the
         cognition's <param>s (null fits nothing), the request bytes a token
         (3 until a reply's usage teaches it fewer), and this call's fitted
         budget and fit. -->
    <data id="max_context_tokens" expr="null"/>
    <data id="completion_reserve_tokens" expr="0"/>
    <data id="bytes_per_token" expr="3"/>
    <data id="budget" expr="null"/>
    <data id="fit" expr="null"/>
    <data id="result" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The dispatch call and the selection being sent (the <foreach>
         items). -->
    <data id="call" expr="null"/>
    <data id="s" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The model call's generated invoke id: a cancelled call's late
         events (still delivered, SCXML 6.4) are not the next call's. -->
    <data id="generate" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Memory: the address of the bot's memory (null: no memory) and the episode and
         directive select, with ?2 the context. The SQL runs on both
         engines (SQLite and Postgres); JSON rows are told by their
         content_format, the 50 most recent by created_at,
         then memory_id (the insertion order), as many of the newest as
         hold at most 24576 characters of content in all (so the memory
         ability's answer stays inside its event bound), read oldest
         first. -->
    <data id="memory" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The id of each request this document last sent the memory, by
         the state that sent it (decision D266). -->
    <data id="memory_requests" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The address of the bot's Embedding ability (null: none, so
         recalling is by recency alone) and the id of each request this
         document last sent it, by the state that sent it. -->
    <data id="embedding" expr="null"/>
    <data id="embedding_requests" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="context_ref" expr="null"/>
    <data id="prior_episodes" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="standing_directives" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- The bot's active learned behaviors, at most 32 by name, which the
         self block names so the bot knows what it does (decision D154). -->
    <data id="behaviors" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="behavior_select" expr="'SELECT name, lifetime, description FROM bot_behavior WHERE status = \'ACTIVE\' ORDER BY name LIMIT 32'"/>
    <data id="statements" expr="[]"/>
    <!-- Recall by association (decision D256, mosfet.py's Associative):
         the cue's vector, what the candidates' select found (the 64
         newest episodes, each with its id, created_at, content length and
         vector, if any; mosfet.py's found), how each is scored (similarity times the cosine with the
         cue plus recency times 0.5 to the power of its age before the
         newest over the half-life, mosfet.py's Weights), and the ids of
         the best that hold at most 24576 characters of content in all,
         null to recall the newest instead. -->
    <data id="cue" expr="null"/>
    <data id="found" expr="null"/>
    <data id="weights" expr="({similarity: 1, recency: 0.35, recency_half_life_ms: 172800000})"/>
    <data id="episode_ids" expr="null"/>
    <data id="candidate_select" expr="'SELECT m.memory_id, CAST(m.created_at AS TEXT), LENGTH(m.content), e.embedding FROM bot_memory m LEFT JOIN bot_memory_embedding e ON e.memory_id = m.memory_id AND e.kind = \'text\' WHERE m.query_tags = ?1 AND (CAST(?2 AS TEXT) IS NULL OR m.context_ref IS NULL OR m.context_ref = ?2) AND m.content_format = \'application/json\' ORDER BY m.created_at DESC, m.memory_id DESC LIMIT 64'"/>
    <data id="episode_select" expr="'SELECT content FROM (SELECT content, created_at, memory_id, SUM(LENGTH(content)) OVER (ORDER BY created_at DESC, memory_id DESC ROWS UNBOUNDED PRECEDING) AS total FROM (SELECT content, created_at, memory_id FROM bot_memory WHERE query_tags = ?1 AND (CAST(?2 AS TEXT) IS NULL OR context_ref IS NULL OR context_ref = ?2) AND content_format = \'application/json\' ORDER BY created_at DESC, memory_id DESC LIMIT 50) AS newest) AS recent WHERE total &lt;= 24576 ORDER BY created_at, memory_id'"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="reasoning.js"/>

  <!-- Between turns: each bot.ability.processing.input is one turn, with
       nothing of the turn before. -->
  <state id="idle">
    <transition event="bot.ability.processing.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.processing.input.json"
                target="recalling">
      <assign location="turn" expr="_event.data.turn"/>
      <assign location="stimulus" expr="_event.data.stimulus"/>
      <assign location="focus" expr="_event.data.focus"/>
      <assign location="focus_candidates" expr="_event.data.focus_candidates"/>
      <assign location="choices" expr="_event.data.choices"/>
      <assign location="held" expr="_event.data.held"/>
      <assign location="environment" expr="_event.data.environment"/>
      <assign location="self" expr="_event.data.self"/>
      <assign location="acted" expr="_event.data.acted"/>
      <assign location="recent" expr="_event.data.recent"/>
      <assign location="max_context_tokens" expr="_event.data.max_context_tokens"/>
      <assign location="completion_reserve_tokens" expr="_event.data.completion_reserve_tokens"/>
      <assign location="bytes_per_token" expr="_event.data.bytes_per_token"/>
      <assign location="system" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="schema" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="prompt" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="prompt_failure" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="images" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="selected" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="handed_on" expr="false"/>
      <assign location="gen_failure" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="rejection" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="attempt" expr="0"/>
      <assign location="last_rejection_key" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="feedback" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="budget" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="fit" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="result" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="context_ref" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="prior_episodes" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="standing_directives" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="behaviors" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="statements" expr="[]"/>
      <assign location="cue" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="found" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="episode_ids" expr="null"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- Recall prior episodes and standing directives, or nothing without
       a memory. -->
  <state id="recalling" initial="recalling_from">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="context_ref" expr="contextRefFromInput()"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="bot.ability.processing.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.processing.input.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The cognition left the turn (cancelled or timed out). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.processing.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.processing.cancel.json"
                target="idle"/>
    <state id="recalling_from">
      <transition cond="hasNoMemory()" target="recalling_nothing"/>
      <transition target="recalling_embedding"/>
    </state>
    <!-- The cue (decision D256): the stimulus's words embedded as a query,
         while the candidates, the newest episodes with their vectors, are
         selected; once both are in, the candidates are ranked against the
         cue and the episodes recalled are the best that fit. A stimulus
         without words, a bot without an Embedding ability, or a cue that
         cannot be embedded, recalls by recency alone. -->
    <state id="recalling_embedding">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="cue" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="found" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="episode_ids" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="candidateSelectStatements()"/>
        <if cond="hasCueWords() &amp;&amp; embedding !== null">
          <send event="bot.ability.embedding.input" targetexpr="embedding" idlocation="embedding_requests.recalling_embedding">
            <content expr="cueEmbeddingInput()"/>
          </send>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.candidates">
            <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.candidates"/>
            <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </onentry>
      <transition cond="hasNoCueWords() || embedding === null" target="recalling_memory"/>
      <transition event="bot.ability.embedding.output" cond="isEmbeddingReply('recalling_embedding')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.embedding.output.json">
        <assign location="cue" expr="_event.data.vectors[0].values"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('candidates')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json">
        <assign location="found" expr="_event.data"/>
      </transition>
      <transition cond="cue !== null &amp;&amp; found !== null" target="recalling_memory">
        <assign location="episode_ids" expr="rankedEpisodeIds(found)"/>
        <log label="reasoning.recall" expr="recallLog(found)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.embedding.failed" cond="isEmbeddingReply('recalling_embedding')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.embedding.failed.json"
                  target="recalling_memory">
        <log label="reasoning.embedding" expr="_event.data.kind"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('candidates')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="done">
        <assign location="result" expr="recallFailedResult(_event.data.message)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="recalling_memory">
        <log label="reasoning.embedding" expr="_event.name"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <state id="recalling_nothing">
      <onentry>
        <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.reasoning.recalled" target="#_internal">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          <param name="host_input" expr="hostInput()"/>
          <param name="prior_episodes" expr="[]"/>
          <param name="memory_consulted" expr="false"/>
          <param name="input" expr="focusInput()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
    </state>
    <state id="recalling_memory">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="statements" expr="episodeSelectStatements()"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="directiveSelectStatements()"/>
        <assign location="statements" expr="behaviorSelectStatements()"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.recall">
          <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.recall"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="statements"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('recall')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json">
        <memory:contents location="prior_episodes" result="_event.data.results[0]"/>
        <memory:contents location="standing_directives" result="_event.data.results[1]"/>
        <assign location="behaviors" expr="recalledBehaviors(_event)"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.reasoning.recalled" target="#_internal">
          <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          <param name="host_input" expr="hostInput()"/>
          <param name="prior_episodes" expr="prior_episodes"/>
          <param name="standing_directives" expr="standing_directives"/>
          <param name="memory_consulted" expr="true"/>
          <param name="input" expr="focusInput()"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('recall')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="done">
        <assign location="result" expr="recallFailedResult(_event.data.message)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="done">
        <assign location="result" expr="recallFailedResult(_event.name)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
    <transition event="bot.ability.reasoning.recalled" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.reasoning.recalled.json"
                cond="hasRecalledWithoutChoices(_event)"
                target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="noChoicesResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.reasoning.recalled" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.reasoning.recalled.json"
                cond="isCurrentTurn(_event)"
                target="applying"/>
  </state>

  <!-- One structured model call; leaving this state cancels it. -->
  <state id="applying">
    <onentry>
      <processing:send location="schema" choices="choices"/>
      <assign location="selected" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="handed_on" expr="false"/>
      <assign location="gen_failure" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="rejection" expr="null"/>
      <assign location="budget" expr="fitBudget()"/>
      <log label="reasoning" expr="choices"/>
      <cognition:model_facing_content location="prompt" failurelocation="prompt_failure"
                                      systemlocation="system" stimulus="stimulus" self="knownSelf()" recent="recent"
                                      environment="environment" acted="acted" prior_episodes="prior_episodes"
                                      standing_directives="standing_directives" feedback="feedback"
                                      instructions="instructions" schema="schema" budget="budget"
                                      held="held" fitlocation="fit" imageslocation="images"/>
      <if cond="isFitted()">
        <log label="cognition.fit" expr="fit"/>
      </if>
    </onentry>
    <!-- Over a prompt budget: fail before the model call is started. -->
    <transition cond="hasNoPrompt()" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="projectionFailedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <invoke idlocation="generate" type="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/services/generate"
            env:apikey="FLOPPY_API_KEY" env:baseurl="FLOPPY_BASE_URL" env:stream="FLOPPY_STREAM">
      <param name="model" expr="model"/>
      <param name="messages" expr="messages()"/>
      <param name="schema" expr="schema"/>
      <param name="schemaname" expr="'dispatch'"/>
      <param name="drafts" expr="drafts()"/>
      <param name="stream" expr="stream"/>
    </invoke>

    <transition event="bot.ability.processing.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.processing.input.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The cognition left the turn (cancelled or timed out). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.processing.cancel" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.processing.cancel.json"
                target="idle"/>
    <!-- A streamed reply's progress goes to the cognition, which bounds this
         stage by inactivity once it streams (decision D101). -->
    <transition event="generate.progress" cond="isCurrent(_event)">
      <send event="generate.progress" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <!-- Every dispatch call's events, in order: each sent to its target
         and kept, but the deliberative handoff, which hands the turn on. -->
    <transition event="generate.result" cond="isCurrent(_event)">
      <assign location="bytes_per_token" expr="observedBytesPerToken(_event)"/>
      <assign location="selected" expr="[]"/>
      <foreach array="_event.data.tool_calls" item="call">
        <foreach array="call.args.events" item="s">
          <if cond="isHandoff(s)">
            <assign location="handed_on" expr="true"/>
          <else/>
            <send eventexpr="s.event" targetexpr="'#_scxml_' + s.target">
              <content expr="selectionData(s)"/>
            </send>
            <assign location="selected[selected.length]" expr="s"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </foreach>
    </transition>
    <transition event="generate.failed" cond="isCurrent(_event)">
      <assign location="gen_failure" expr="generateFailure(_event)"/>
      <assign location="rejection" expr="rejectionOf(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="isCurrent(_event) &amp;&amp; hasSelection()" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="selectedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- A rejected selection is repaired: the call is made again with the
         rejection as its feedback, unless it is the same rejection twice
         running or the repairs are spent. -->
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="isCurrent(_event) &amp;&amp; isRepairable()" target="applying">
      <log label="reasoning.repair" expr="repairLog()"/>
      <assign location="attempt" expr="attempt + 1"/>
      <assign location="last_rejection_key" expr="rejection.key"/>
      <assign location="feedback" expr="repairFeedback()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="isCurrent(_event) &amp;&amp; isRejected()" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="rejectedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke" cond="isCurrent(_event)" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="failedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.*" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="couldNotRunResult(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- A draft of a selection still being written (decision D262): any
         other event the call returns is one, named by its event's marker,
         and goes to the one target that offers the drafted event; a draft
         whose event more than one target offers is dropped. -->
    <transition event="*" cond="isDraft(_event)">
      <send eventexpr="_event.name" targetexpr="'#_scxml_' + draftTarget(_event)">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The turn's answer to the cognition, then the next turn. -->
  <state id="done">
    <onentry>
      <send event="bot.ability.processing.output" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="withFit(result)"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <transition target="idle"/>
  </state>
</scxml>
